    "problem_statement": "QR code rendering fails with certain module drawers\n\nDescription\n\nI'm trying to generate QR codes with different styled module drawers, but some of them are failing to render properly.\n\nWhen using HorizontalBarsDrawer, RoundedModuleDrawer, or VerticalBarsDrawer, the QR code generation fails, while other drawers like CircleModuleDrawer, GappedSquareModuleDrawer, and SquareModuleDrawer work fine.\n\nHow to reproduce:\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image.styledpil import StyledPilImage\nfrom qrcode.image.styles import moduledrawers\nimport io\n\n# This works fine\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, module_drawer=moduledrawers.SquareModuleDrawer())\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())\n\n# This fails\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, module_drawer=moduledrawers.HorizontalBarsDrawer())\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())\n```\n\nThe issue seems to be related to how the module boundaries are checked. The QR code generation works fine with some module drawers but fails with others that might be accessing the modules in a different way."
